codex
The constructed family now passes the basic algebra check on all four presets. It stays native: the solver receives \(R=\mathbb F_p[t,x]/(h(t)x)\), \(I=(x)\), and the paper’s determinant recurrence, then returns the irreducible polynomials that specify the primary components. At the shipping preset the answer is 31 linear polynomials (62 scalar atoms, 581 characters in the first audit), while the candidate space is about \(2^{1241}\). I’m running the full adversary, factorer, relabelling, and 200,000-sample gates now.
