+    report["all_passed"] = all(
+        value.get("pass") is True
+        for key, value in report.items()
+        if key.startswith("G") and isinstance(value, dict))
+    return report
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    print(json.dumps(selftest(), indent=2, sort_keys=True))

codex
A useful refinement came out of the cost audit: 31 factors were unnecessary. Holding the answer at 15 factors still leaves a roughly \(2^{580}\) structure-aware space. The standard factorer used 963,024 counted operations across eight trials (120,378 average), while the compact route drops to about 125 field operations and the answer to roughly 75 tokens. I’m tightening the shipping family to that smaller witness so failures are less attributable to transcription or raw arithmetic.
apply patch
